# Manager view baseline (5/29/26)

Treat the **Manager view** as frozen at the **last commit on 5/29/2026** — `1a3a23d` (10:09), not the earlier `9f9a527` (10:02). Later commits may change shared data files; do **not** change Manager files unless the user asks.

| 5/29 commit | Time | Manager impact |
|-------------|------|----------------|
| `9f9a527` | 10:02 | Tier deal books, rotation workflow, queue badges (`manager-view.js`, `ManagerView.html`) |
| `1a3a23d` | 10:09 | Pink rotation alert cards (`manager-view.css`) — **baseline** |

## Do not re-apply (6/2/26 work — rejected)

Unless the user **explicitly** asks to change the Manager view again, do **not** add or restore:

- `manager-view/manager-projects.js`
- **Project Management** tab (`tab-projects`, `view-projects`) in `ManagerView.html`
- Manager imports of `shared/projects-data.js` or `shared/lead-view.css`
- Manager wiring to `ProjectsData`, `renderManagerProjects()`, or `countRegionalProjects()` in `manager-view/manager-view.js`
- Manager-specific project panel CSS in `manager-view/manager-view.css`

## In scope for Manager work

When editing Manager files, match patterns already on `main` at 5/29:

- Roster, Deal Assignment Review, Reporting tabs
- `manager-view/manager-view.js`, `reporting.js`, `reporting-data.js`
- Shared team data via `TeamData` / `ic-sync` as already wired on 5/29

## Out of scope (unless user overrides this rule)

- Porting Team Lead **Project Management** UI or logic into Manager
- Assuming Manager has org-project roster / sponsor “My Projects” features

## Team Lead is separate

`LeadView.html`, `shared/lead-view.js`, `shared/lead-view.css`, and `shared/projects-data.js` are the Team Lead surface. Changes there do **not** imply Manager should be updated to match.

## If Manager files drift

Restore Manager tracked files from git baseline:

```bash
git restore ManagerView.html manager-view/
rm -f manager-view/manager-projects.js
```
